---
title: BA's Best Fried Chicken Sandwich
description: This fried chicken sandwich is engineered for maximum impact. Each element is awesome, but the way they come together puts it over the top.
course: dinner
cuisine: american
servings: 1
author: Claire Saffitz
source: https://www.bonappetit.com/recipe/bas-best-fried-chicken-sandwich
prep time: 30 minutes
cook time: 20 minutes
tags:
  - american
  - dinner
  - fried
  - chicken
  - sandwich
---

> This recipe is designed to make one large sandwich. Adjust ingredient quantities as needed for more servings.

==Seasoning==
Mix @kosher salt{1%tbsp}, @light brown sugar{1%tsp}, and @baking powder{1%tsp} in a small bowl. Season @chicken thighs{4}(skin-on or skinless, boneless) all over with salt mixture (you won’t need all of it). Chill uncovered on a wire rack set inside a rimmed baking sheet, at least 2 hours and up to 1 day.

==Seasoned Mayonnaise==
Combine @garlic{1%clove}(finely grated) and @lemon juice{2%tbsp} in a medium bowl; let sit 10 minutes. Mix in @mayonnaise{1/2%cup}, @chives{2%tbsp}(finely chopped), @celery seeds{1/2%tsp}, and @black pepper{1/2%tsp}; season with @kosher salt{}.

==Assembly==
Whisk @all-purpose flour{1 1/2%cups}, @cornstarch{1/3%cup}, @garlic powder{1%tbsp}, @onion powder{1%tbsp}, @paprika{1%tbsp}, @cayenne pepper{2%tsp}, and @kosher salt{2%tbsp} in a medium bowl. Whisk @egg{1}(beaten to blend), @buttermilk{1%cup}, @bourbon{2%tbsp}(optional), and @hot sauce{3%tbsp}(such as Frank's) in another medium bowl. Working with 1 piece at a time, dredge chicken in flour mixture, turning to coat and packing into crevices. Shake to remove excess; return to rack. Pour 3 Tbsp. buttermilk mixture into flour mixture and work in with your fingers. Dip chicken into remaining buttermilk mixture, allow excess to drip off, then pack moistened flour mixture firmly onto chicken. Gently shake off excess; return to rack. Chill at least 30 minutes and up to 12 hours.

==Frying==
Pour @peanut oil{8%cups}(or vegetable oil) into a large heavy pot fitted with thermometer to come halfway up sides. Heat over medium-high until thermometer registers 350°. Working in 2 batches, fry chicken, turning often and adjusting heat to maintain temperature, until deep golden brown, 5–8 minutes per batch. Transfer to a wire rack set over paper towels to drain.

==Toasting Buns==
Heat a dry large skillet, preferably cast iron, over medium. Brush cut sides of @hamburger buns{4} with @unsalted butter{3%tbsp} and, working in batches, cook, cut side down, until deep golden brown, about 2 minutes per batch.

==Assembly==
Mix 1 Tbsp. @pickle brine{} into 2 Tbsp. seasoned mayonnaise in a medium bowl. Add @iceberg lettuce{4%cups}(thinly sliced), season with @kosher salt{} and @black pepper{}, and toss to coat. Spread some seasoned mayonnaise over cut sides of buns. Build sandwiches with pickles, fried chicken, slaw, and more hot sauce, if desired.
